diagnosis_text:
The Campus 1-to-backbone outage is not due to a physical link failure between mswitch0 and router16. The L1/L2 links are healthy: ethtool reports “Link detected: yes” on mswitch0 eth0 and eth1 and router16 eth0 and eth1; both are slaves in bond0 with MII Status: up on each side (cat /proc/net/bonding/bond0). mswitch0 can ping router16 (10.2.2.1) successfully, proving the r16_ms0/r16_ms0_2 bond is passing traffic.

The actual fault is a control-plane failure on router16: FRRouting is down (systemctl on router16: “Active: failed”), and its running config is empty—no OSPF. Consequently, router16 has only connected routes (10.2.2.0/24 and 172.30.1.0/24) and does not learn/advertise backbone routes. mswitch0’s OSPF show
